{"serves":2,"prepMinutes":25,"cookMinutes":210,"ingredients":[{"id":"lamb-shoulder","quantity":"700g","note":"bone-in or boneless, trimmed of excess fat"},{"id":"sushi-rice","quantity":"200g","note":"rinsed until the water runs clear"},{"id":"fresh-ginger","quantity":"60g","note":"peeled, half sliced and half finely grated"},{"id":"enoki-mushroom","quantity":"100g","note":"base trimmed, strands separated"},{"id":"pickled-turnips","quantity":"80g","note":"sliced into thin batons"},{"id":"sesame-seeds","quantity":"2 tbsp","note":"toasted in a dry pan"},{"id":"giant-puffball","quantity":"150g","note":"cut into 1cm slices"},{"id":"fromage-frais","quantity":"100g","note":"to serve"},{"id":"cooking-oil","quantity":"2 tbsp","note":""},{"id":"butter","quantity":"20g","note":""},{"id":"black-pepper","quantity":"1/2 tsp","note":"freshly ground"},{"id":"salt","quantity":"1 1/2 tsp","note":""},{"id":"water","quantity":"about 500ml","note":"for the roasting tin and the rice"}],"steps":[{"text":"Heat the oven to 160C (140C fan). Rub the lamb shoulder all over with 1 tbsp cooking oil, 1 tsp salt and the black pepper. Scatter the sliced fresh ginger in a small roasting tin and sit the lamb on top. Pour in 150ml water.","minutes":10,"uses":["lamb-shoulder","fresh-ginger","cooking-oil","salt","black-pepper","water"]},{"text":"Cover the tin tightly with foil and roast for 3 hours, until the lamb is completely tender and pulls apart with a fork. Remove the foil for the final 30 minutes so the top browns and the juices reduce.","minutes":210,"uses":["lamb-shoulder","fresh-ginger"]},{"text":"Rest the lamb for 15 minutes, then shred it with two forks, discarding any excess fat. Stir the shredded meat through the ginger-flavoured juices in the tin and keep warm under foil.","minutes":15,"uses":["lamb-shoulder","fresh-ginger"]},{"text":"Rinse the sushi rice in several changes of cold water until it runs clear. Put it in a lidded pan with 260ml water and 1/2 tsp salt, bring to the boil, then cover, reduce to the lowest heat and cook for 12 minutes. Rest, covered, for 10 minutes off the heat.","minutes":22,"uses":["sushi-rice","water","salt"]},{"text":"Heat the remaining oil in a frying pan over a medium-high heat. Fry the giant puffball slices for 2 to 3 minutes each side until golden and crisp at the edges. Season lightly with salt and set aside.","minutes":6,"uses":["giant-puffball","cooking-oil","salt"]},{"text":"Wipe the pan, melt the butter over a high heat and add the enoki mushroom with the grated fresh ginger. Toss for 1 minute until just wilted. Take off the heat straight away.","minutes":2,"uses":["enoki-mushroom","butter","fresh-ginger"]},{"text":"Divide the warm rice between two bowls. Pile the shredded lamb on top with a spoonful of its juices, then add the puffball, enoki and pickled turnips. Scatter over the sesame seeds and finish each bowl with a spoonful of fromage frais.","minutes":null,"uses":["sushi-rice","lamb-shoulder","giant-puffball","enoki-mushroom","pickled-turnips","sesame-seeds","fromage-frais"]}],"tips":["Toast the sesame seeds in a dry pan for a minute until fragrant, then tip them out at once so they do not burn.","If the juices in the tin look thin after shredding, spoon them into a small pan and boil briskly for a few minutes to concentrate them.","Keep the enoki cooking brief so it stays silky and does not turn rubbery."]}
